etween the mages and the  templars you'll see that right here  mages and Templars are kind of going at  it down there but we'll take you to less  explored areas frostback mountains out  into out into bogs and deep desert what  the thing is is that for Dragon Age  Inquisition the scope of the story is so  big that we needed the breadth of  terrain we we're crossing two nations so  we couldn't just have one region we  needed to be able to pull it out and  just have it be able to go where it  needed to go from the  retelling perspective so one of the  tricky things about you know big open  games is that scale alone doesn't make  things interesting you need that  emergent gameplay and all the little  in-between areas when you're not doing a  critical mission so in terms of what you  guys are doing with Inquisition what's  the incentive to just explore and take  things at your own pace yeah I mean  you're absolutely right about about  open-world gameplay for us what we  really make sure is that every area you  go to is important to the story you're  doing things to further the the power of  the Inquisition this is an organization  that you ultimately lead and it gives  you the power to do things you wouldn't  otherwise be able to do you reach a  fortress the doors are locked behind you  you can't sneak in the back you have you  have troops you 100 guys that you can  use to bash the door and to get you  through that front door and ultimately  what you're doing the exploration is  things that are either going to make you  better  so gathering crafting materials in order  to make yourself better armor and arms  or you're doing things that are actually  furthering the renown and power of the  Inquisition to draw people to your cause  all right so we're starting to get quite  a flood of questions here  Maximillian on twitter is asking about  the controls in the game because you  know from Dragon Age Origins to Dragon  Age 2 you guys quicken the pace a little  bit may the action a little bit more  immediate and quick what are you guys  doing with Inquisition so we're doing  two things there it were we're slowing  down the animation to be a little more  weight a little bit more grounded in the  world so when a guys swinging a  two-handed sword he's not spinning  around as much yeah  he's a little bit more grounded the  other thing is is that we're bringing  back tactile camera on all five  platforms so it was just on PC for  Dragon Age Origins didn't exist on  Dragon Age 2 at all here you're going to  be able to pull the camera back really  look at the battlefield consider what  you're doing  and and really give those that really  fine control if you want to do that  you'll also be able to control the game  completely in real time if if that's a  playstyle you prefer now what is the  reason behind bringing that tactical  camera back is it just something that  you are able to do now that you got more  time and you can fine-tune it  yeah it's partially that it's partially  just that ultimately this is a game mode  leadership this is a game about  about controlling a group both the  Inquisition but also your party and they  just felt very much even just from a  storytelling thematic respect it was a  very appropriate thing to bring back all  right let's see here a lot of a lot of  questions about romance options yeah we  always get a lot of questions about  romance options so let's just just  describe it in a nutshell because  Bioware has always been very progressive  about that type of thing and giving just  players options and not forcing them to  live their character in a very  particular way I mean that I think  options are is a very good way to put it  we definitely want to make sure that you  have as much control over the way you  play your character and the way you  interact with other people so that does  mean romances are totally optional  you're not we're going to try to make it  as clear as possible when you're when  you're crossing that line so you're not  stumbling into a romantic option by out  by mistake all right yeah I mean I still  remember in Dragon Age Origins and this  might be too but Dragon Age Origins  walking into the brothel them asking  what you prefer male or female what the  third option was surprised me yes so  it's always been that kind of game yes  let's see here if some questions about  importing saves from previous games so  the way that works is a Dragon Age  Inquisition is definitely a great place  to pick up the series if you haven't  played before the wait what we're doing  is we have a web service called the  Dragon Age key which you can go to and  actually build a save essentially build  your choices from the previous two games  using an interactive form it's amazing  closed beta right now we're going to be  expanding that out over the summer  all right so and is that give you kind  of like a little story primer in case I  forget it was details exactly if you  really want to be brought if you haven't  played dragon before and you really  really want to be a up-to-date on the on  the world the Dragon Age keep is going  to give you an opportunity to really  figure seeing what happened in the  previous two games all right so we're  actually taking a look at a big epic  dragon battle right now yeah we'd be  remiss if we didn't talk about that a  little bit yeah so I mean I think we  actually were distracted we're kind of  actually pretty hard  yeah so I mean dragons are dragons are  actually the biggest baddest things  they're really endgame content they're  apex predators you really need to bring  your game when you're going to fight  them they one thing we've introduced for  Dragon Age Inquisition is multiple  target regions so now you're not just  attacking a big sort of sphere of damage  you can attack their legs if you do  enough damage they're going to roll over  onto their side giving you access to  their head to really to really do a lot  more damage so and you said that they  are endgame enemies what type of enemies  are we going to be encountering along  the progression sword strike oh one of  the things we're doing in in this game  is we're not Auto balancing the game  which means like in the in the very  first area in there's ad right there  will be a dragon there and if you want  to go and try to take them on at level 5  you can do that it's probably going to  be a bad idea but we're going to really  open up and make it leave it to the  player to really decide what they deeply  want to engage a lot of a lot of  humanoid creatures obviously this is  very much a game that has a lot of  people and politics in it but the game  at its fundamental core is about this  breach in the sky which spitting demons  out so a lot of demons you're going to  see over the course of the game all  right now abdel-rahman  cash on Twitter is asking about types of  dragons variety is it sort of like just  that one singular dragon in the distance  that you're working towards or is it  sort of various types there are various  types of dragons we actually have dragon  legs as well sort of the younger dragons  but we'll be doing dragons differentiate  by element like essentially like fire  breath or ice breath as well as a few  other sort of regional variations based  on where in the world you actually are  all right let's see so many very very  specific questions about Dragon Age  that's the kind of community that you  guys that's the community we have he has  very specific questions about about Lily  Anna's haircut or something else right  yes so how do you filter that kind of  stuff how do you take just that wealth  of feedback from the community  and use that to inform the direction of  the game yeah I mean it's really  important to be open to these kinds of  questions and and to try to respond as  best we can obviously we don't want to  answer questions that are going to spoil  the story I mean even though you people  think they want the answer some of these  questions there's some that the answer  is not going to be it's going to it's  going to wreck things for them so we  have to be careful about what we do and  do not answer right right of course  let's see we're getting questions about  platforms of the game specifically what  we're seeing here can you tell do you  have to know what platform this is yeah  so this was actually captured on a PC  with a with a controller we will have  full PC mouse and keyboard controls as  well and then and then and then like  Xbox one and ps4 will have really high  graphical fidelity as well ps3 and  xbox360 are obviously going to have a  little bit lag behind a little bit there  yeah yeah  any plans for modding support on the PC  version um  maybe we've talked about it obviously  this game uses frostbite 3 so that's  something that doesn't currently exist  for that engine but it is something we  have talked about and so not at launch  right and even if it's not official the  Dragon Age community tends to be pretty  active they'll they'll definitely figure  it out we've seen Dragon Age 2 stuff  where we didn't have an official toolset  that it has shown up for sure let's see  uh what  so okay so we talked about the importing  of Saves and how you guys are building  that tool to create your own save file  in case you don't have that on you know  in case you don't have that anymore but  in terms of what you're importing how  much does that affect the events of  Dragon Age Inquisition Jared Richard on  Twitter is actually asking about this  yeah so one thing that Dragon Age has  always been about it's much more about  the world and the time than it is about  a specific character so the what that  means is the really there's there's  there's sort of choices you've made that  matter for the world choices you've made  that matter for characters and those are  very important so you know who's the  king from Dragon Age Origins that's  really important ultimately who the  warden romanced that's actually  important too because we have characters  the return it's important that to know  if Morgan we had a relationship with  that with that warden character but some  of the other choices you made  maybe we're mattered in the moments but  didn't matter over to the overall state  of the world so we're importing hundreds  of choices from the previous games so  it's a lot all right Marc well I  appreciate your time and I'd like to  apologize to the 900 people whose  questions we didn't get to - yeah I mean  we'll try to answer them as best we can  all right great so there you guys have  it that was your look at Dragon Age  Inquisition courtesy of our friend Marc  Terra from Bioware

